## Working method

- Establish context before changing code: goal, constraints, and how the existing
  code already solves nearby problems. Look for reuse before writing new code.
- Ground every change in the current code: re-read the files you will touch and
  confirm the symbols you call exist. Specs, handoffs and summaries can be stale.
- State the intended change and its expected outcome before editing.
- Break work into small, verifiable steps; land each as its own commit.
- Verify each step with the narrowest check, then widen before finishing (see
  Validation commands).
- The maintainer owns decisions. Propose new ones in the decision log as
  Proposed; its authority rules say when an entry becomes Accepted.

